  <title>Trial balance</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Reports</gui><gui>Financial</gui><gui>Trial
  balance</gui></guiseq> lists every account with its <gui>Opening</gui>
  balance, the period's <gui>Debits</gui> and <gui>Credits</gui>, and its
  <gui>Closing</gui> balance. It starts with the current fiscal year. Choose
  other dates with the icons in <gui>From :</gui> and <gui>To :</gui>, and click
  <gui>Reload</gui>.</p>

  <p>Balances are signed: debit balances are positive and credit balances
  negative, so revenue, liability and equity accounts show negative. There
  are no year end closing entries, so a revenue or expense account's opening
  balance is its total since the books began, not zero.</p>

  <p>Under the list, a sentence says whether the books are in balance. When
  they are not, it says by how much, and whether the difference arose in this
  period or was already there at its start. To find the entries responsible,
  use <link xref="unbalanced_transactions"/>.</p>

  <p>Check <gui>Hide accounts with no activity and no balance</gui> to shorten
  the list; the totals still count every account. <gui>Report hub</gui>
  exports it; see <link xref="report_hub"/>.</p>

</page>
